{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PAUSED for the operator's Claude peak-usage window (5-11am PT). Recording exact state.\n\nDID NOT PUSH ps4, deliberately. The pause instruction was \"push if the attestation refresh\nhas completed and the push is the only step left.\" It has NOT completed (the run is still\nin flight, zero output), and `review-plan --status` reports `stale-material` — my last plan\nedits (description 7991 -> 7967 chars, file_impact 8 -> 9 paths) invalidated the signature.\n\nPushing anyway would have been actively counterproductive, not merely premature: ps4 is not\na trivial rebase, so the `LLM-Review+1` currently copied onto ps3 would NOT carry over. It\nwould trigger a fresh code review, which runs the bugfix-size-attestation check (this change\nis 211 non-test lines, over the 150-line bug-fix floor), which would read the stale\nattestation and vote -1 — burning a review-bot LLM call and a full CI cycle during exactly\nthe window the pause exists to protect.\n\nEXACT STATE\n\nWorktree: /Users/joeoakhart/grayling-acli-cancel  (branch grayling-acli-cancel, clean)\nLocal HEAD: b20afb53b3 \"Count cancelled link deletes as failed\", 9 files,\n+554/-137, rebased onto origin/main c6e71440b5.\nGerrit: change 1655, currently at patch set 3 (e85628abbe).\n  - ps3 has LLM-Review+1 (earned on ps2, copied forward).\n  - ps3 CI will FAIL, and that is expected//already-diagnosed: it predates the local fix\n    below. Do not re-triage it from scratch.\n\nWHAT ps3 IS MISSING (the only delta in local HEAD vs ps3):\n`.github/complexity-baseline.json` - one line removed. Extracting `_dispatch_link_removes`\ndropped `_update_one_dispatch_links` under the C901 threshold, so its baseline entry went\nSTALE. `--check` tolerates stale (exit 0) which is why I missed it first pass, but\n`tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` requires the committed baseline to be clean and\nfails on it. Removed with `check_complexity_baseline.py --update-stale`. A removal is an\nimprovement, so `--lock` still passes (\"OK (no raised ceilings or new entries)\").\n\nGATES, all green locally on b20afb53b3:\n  make lint (ruff + format + complexity baseline: active=60 new=0 increased=0 stale=0)\n  make typecheck (506 files)\n  --lock vs origin/main: OK\n  tests/unit/rebar_reconciler: 2413 passed\n  tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py: 72 passed\n  module sizes: dispatch_one 655, dispatch_apply_phases 595 (cap 800)\n\nNEXT STEP, in this order, after 11:05am PT:\n1. Check the in-flight `review-plan` refresh; if it did not certify, re-run it. Verify\n   `review-plan satisfied-emerald-grayling --status` reports ok/certified BEFORE pushing.\n   Do NOT edit the description or file_impact again after that point - every such edit\n   re-stales the attestation the size gate depends on. That ordering trap cost two CI cycles.\n2. `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main` from the worktree -> ps4.\n3. Await LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1.\n4. Submit (POST /a/changes/1655/submit -d '{}'), then ff the worktree.\n5. Tick the 8 AC checkboxes (checkbox state is attestation-SAFE, it is normalized out of\n   the fingerprint, so ticking cannot stale the signature).\n6. `transition satisfied-emerald-grayling in_progress closed --class preexisting`\n   (the miscount predates the runs that surfaced it and predates change 1640 entirely).\n\nI let the already-running review-plan finish rather than killing it: it started before the\npause, and aborting would waste the capacity already spent AND force a second full run\nlater, costing more total peak capacity than letting the one in flight complete."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786535565300343001,"uuid":"78cc6bd1-feaa-457b-be42-839ea69ffa93"}